    "summary": "Smoky Box of Rain, The Other One > Wharf Rat & a soaring Playin' jam",
    "blurb": "The set delivers a fiery Box of Rain and an inspired The Other One → Wharf Rat transition, culminating in a soaring Playing In The Band jam. Jerry’s vocals and guitar shine while Keith adds jazzy, spiraling fills. Overall soundboard capture is excellent with only minor hiss.",
    "review": "Winterland on October 9, 1972 finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. From the opening of Set 1, the band rides a tight groove into a luminous Box of Rain that showcases Jerry’s powerful vocals and pristine guitar tone. The China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue rolls smoothly into a mellow Mexicali Blues before the set peaks with Playing In The Band, where Bob Weir’s lead lines take on an otherworldly edge and Keith Godchaux spirals through jazzy fills that feel among his wildest of the era. Set 2 erupts with a classic Truckin' → The Other One → Wharf Rat suite; the transition is electric, and the jam builds into a breathtaking Playing In The Band climax that still feels fresh decades later. Sugar Magnolia adds a bright finish before a raucous encore of Johnny B. Goode. The Vernon soundboard recording captures this fire‑filled night with crystal‑clear separation and just enough hiss to remind you it’s a 1972 tape, making it the definitive listen for anyone wanting the full Winterland experience.",
